{"data":{"id":"10.48550/arxiv.2603.07540","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2603.07540","prefix":"10.48550","suffix":"arxiv.2603.07540","identifiers":[{"identifier":"2603.07540","identifierType":"arXiv"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"alternateIdentifierType":"arXiv","alternateIdentifier":"2603.07540"}],"creators":[{"name":"Chen, Haoyu","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Haoyu","familyName":"Chen","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Liu, Qing","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Qing","familyName":"Liu","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Zhou, Yuqian","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Yuqian","familyName":"Zhou","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Zhang, He","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"He","familyName":"Zhang","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Wang, Zhaowen","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Zhaowen","familyName":"Wang","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Ren, Mengwei","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Mengwei","familyName":"Ren","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Ren, Jingjing","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Jingjing","familyName":"Ren","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Wang, Xiang","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Xiang","familyName":"Wang","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Lin, Zhe","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Zhe","familyName":"Lin","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Zhu, Lei","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Lei","familyName":"Zhu","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]}],"titles":[{"title":"How Long Can Unified Multimodal Models Generate Images Reliably? Taming Long-Horizon Interleaved Image Generation via Context Curation"}],"publisher":"arXiv","container":{},"publicationYear":2026,"subjects":[{"lang":"en","subject":"Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV)","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"lang":"en","subject":"Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"subject":"FOS: Computer and information sciences","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"},{"subject":"FOS: Computer and information sciences","schemeUri":"http://www.oecd.org/science/inno/38235147.pdf","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"}],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2026-03-08T09:01:20Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2026-03-10T01:08:06Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2026-03","dateType":"Available","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2026","dateType":"Issued"}],"language":null,"types":{"ris":"GEN","bibtex":"misc","citeproc":"article","schemaOrg":"CreativeWork","resourceType":"Article","resourceTypeGeneral":"Preprint"},"relatedIdentifiers":[],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"1","rightsList":[{"rights":"arXiv.org perpetual, non-exclusive license","rightsUri":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/"}],"descriptions":[{"description":"Unified multimodal models hold the promise of generating extensive, interleaved narratives, weaving text and imagery into coherent long-form stories. However, current systems suffer from a critical reliability gap: as sequences grow, generation quality rapidly collapses. In this work, we investigate the mechanism behind this failure and argue that it is distinct from standard long-context challenges. We reveal that in generation, accumulated visual history acts as a source of active pollution, a decay governed specifically by the number of image events rather than raw token count. We identify a structural vulnerability where dense visual tokens overwhelm the attention mechanism, creating noise that distorts future synthesis. Guided by these mechanistic insights, we propose UniLongGen, a training-free inference strategy that prioritizes safe conditioning over total recall. Instead of retaining all history, UniLongGen dynamically curates the model's memory, identifying and discarding interfering visual signals based on the model's own internal relevance rankings. Extensive experiments demonstrate that this active forgetting approach is essential for stability: UniLongGen significantly outperforms baselines in long-horizon fidelity and consistency, while simultaneously reducing memory footprint and inference time.","descriptionType":"Abstract"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"xml":"","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.07540","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":0,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"mds","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"viewsOverTime":[],"downloadCount":0,"downloadsOverTime":[],"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":0,"citationsOverTime":[],"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":0,"versionOfCount":0,"created":"2026-03-10T04:10:05.000Z","registered":"2026-03-10T04:10:06.000Z","published":"2026","updated":"2026-03-10T04:10:06.000Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"arxiv.content","type":"clients"}},"provider":{"data":{"id":"arxiv","type":"providers"}},"media":{"data":{"id":"10.48550/arxiv.2603.07540","type":"media"}},"references":{"data":[]},"citations":{"data":[]},"parts":{"data":[]},"partOf":{"data":[]},"versions":{"data":[]},"versionOf":{"data":[]}}}}